Z||000002||FieroLT1||09-24-2001||07:32 AM||||I had never worked on a car before in my entire life, with the exception of changing a spare tire.<BR>And look what I was able to do.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A> <P>"You can do anything you put your mind to"<BR>BTW: Site lists some tools needed too.<P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||09-24-2001||07:37 AM||||i'm in close to the same boat, but i wouldn't rule it out. i'm considering it just a matter of time. <P>right now archies got the $4k swap thread going. plus i've been to his site and read over it a few times (along with bubbajoes for the caddy swap [even got some of his mounts since they were cheap], and even any northstar stuff i can find).<P> i recently got my hoist together and tried it (pulled an old 4cyl out). picked up an engine stand at a yard sale, and now i'm keeping an eye out for a nice big floor jack. i think those things will make it physically posible to do it.<P>a few years back i learned enough welding to do what would be required. i don't have one but if i get that far i could try to get it to work, plus i'm looking out for a deal on one of those too. i want one for other projects anyway.   <P>i didn't come from a family of car hobbiests so i've been picking up what i can over the years (and checking here a lot 'cause these people know stuff) along with the basic tools that i would need and doing any repairs i'm capable of. <P>so if you're asking "can i pull it off like, this weekend?", you might be biting off more than you can chew, but if you have time to work at it i wouldn't want to dampen your spirits. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000004||KissMySSFiero||09-24-2001||08:26 AM||||Like fieroLT1 said anyone can do it if they put theyre mind to it.  however how much time do you want to put into the project.  He took 3 years.  arey ou willling to do this.  if you take your time and ask questions as you go i see no reason why not.  there are a lot of people on the forum who have done this swap,  ask them what they did to make it easier as you go.  <BR>as far as cheap v-8's...that depends on what you think of as cheap.  cheap to me would be getting a new LM1 motor for $1300 and putting a tpi fuel injection on it.  total with wiring running about $2000.   good luck on yoru project.  keep us updated<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
